<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24376" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημητριάς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>,
			ἡ, fem. Adj.: <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλή</span>)
			tribe <i>named in honour of Demetrius Poliorcetes,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Demetr.</u>
				10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> city founded
			by him, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				3.6.4
			</span></i>, etc.:—hence <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δημητριεῖς</span></b> , οἱ, its citizens,
				<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				5.99.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> as
				Subst., <i>six-rowed barley,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περιστερεὼν ὕπτιος</span>
			, Ps.-<i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				4.60
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
